    <string name="battery_guide_title_generic">Steps for your phone</string>
    <string name="battery_open_app_settings">Open app settings</string>
    <string name="battery_open_web_guide">See the web guide</string>
    <string name="battery_steps_samsung">1. Tap “Open app settings” › Battery › choose “Unrestricted”.\n2. In Settings › Device care (or Battery and device care) › Battery › Background usage limits: remove this app from “Sleeping apps” and “Deep sleeping apps”, and add it to “Never sleeping apps”.</string>
    <string name="battery_steps_motorola">1. Tap “Open app settings” › Battery › choose “Unrestricted” (on some models: “Battery optimization” › “Don’t optimize”).\n2. If it still disappears, check in Settings › Battery that Battery Saver is not always on.</string>
    <string name="battery_steps_xiaomi">1. Tap “Open app settings” and turn on “Autostart”.\n2. In “Battery saver”, choose “No restrictions”.\n3. In “Other permissions”, turn on “Display pop-up windows while running in the background” and “Show on Lock screen”.\n4. In the recent apps view, long-press this app and tap the lock so it is not closed.</string>
    <string name="battery_steps_other">Tap “Open app settings” › Battery and choose “Unrestricted” or “Don’t optimize”. Each brand names it differently: the web guide has the steps for yours.</string>

